Add a product to Ads Studio - under a brand, or with no brand at all - from its page link and/or a pasted description. Answers as soon as the row is queued - Ads Studio reads the page in the background. Do not poll and do not list products to check. Read ads_studio_get_product when the user asks about it. Use this when the research missed a product or the user names a new one. To refresh an existing product from its page, pass its id in overwrite instead of adding a second row.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield_ads_studio_add_product(args: {
  // The brand this product belongs to, from ads_studio_list_brands. Leave it out for a product of no brand: it is still listed by ads_studio_list_products without brand_id and can be generated.
  brand_id?: string;
  // Product photo URLs the user supplied or uploaded. Ads Studio fetches each one, so a link it cannot reach is refused.
  images?: Array<string>;
  // Existing product ids to refresh from the page instead of creating a new row.
  overwrite?: Array<string>;
  // The user's own description, when there is no page or it adds facts the page lacks.
  text?: string;
  // The product's own page. Give this whenever the user has it: it is what makes the ads specific.
  url?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Plans supported by Ads Studio.
  allowed_plans?: Array<string>;
  brand_id?: string;
  // Credits available when the request was refused.
  credits_have?: number;
  // Credits required for the refused request.
  credits_needed?: number;
  // Credits missing for the refused request.
  credits_short?: number;
  error?: string;
  error_code?: string;
  // The concurrent-generation limit when the queue was full.
  limit?: number;
  next_step?: string;
  // The account's current plan when access was refused.
  plan?: string;
  products?: Array<{ product_id?: string; status?: string; }>;
  // The queued generation count when the queue was full.
  queued?: number;
}>>; };
```

