Research a brand from its website and build its Ads Studio brand profile: products, palette, logo, tone and audience, read from the live site. Pass the website when you have it - with a URL the research starts at once and takes a few minutes; with only a name Ads Studio answers with the site it thinks was meant and starts nothing, so confirm that with the user and call again with the URL. This reads the brand's own public website. It does not design logos or brand assets (that is the brand-asset-creation workflow) and it is not the Marketing Studio brand-kit record (marketing_create_brand_kit). Before the first Ads Studio call in a conversation, load the Ads Studio instructions with get_preset_instructions and preset 'ads-studio'.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield_ads_studio_create_brand(args: {
  // The brand's website URL, or its name if the user has not given a URL.
  input: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Plans supported by Ads Studio.
  allowed_plans?: Array<string>;
  brand_id?: string;
  // Credits available when the request was refused.
  credits_have?: number;
  // Credits required for the refused request.
  credits_needed?: number;
  // Credits missing for the refused request.
  credits_short?: number;
  error?: string;
  error_code?: string;
  // The concurrent-generation limit when the queue was full.
  limit?: number;
  needs_confirmation?: boolean;
  next_step?: string;
  // The account's current plan when access was refused.
  plan?: string;
  // The queued generation count when the queue was full.
  queued?: number;
  // True when the research is running; false when a website is still needed.
  started?: boolean;
  suggested_brand_name?: string;
  suggested_website?: string;
}>>; };
```

