Generate ad creatives in Ads Studio: for a brand, for products of any brand or of none, or from a prompt and the user's pictures alone, with or without the brand kit. Ads Studio writes the concepts and renders the pictures. This spends Higgsfield credits, so quote with ads_studio_quote and get explicit approval of the exact allocation and credit cost first. An approval from the Ads Studio app allocation is NOT approval. When allocation is supplied, this tool quotes the whole allocation and requests native MCP form confirmation when supported. Otherwise it returns approval_required and credits: show the exact counts and cost, ask for explicit chat approval and stop. Only after approval, repeat the unchanged allocation with expected_credits. Never split the allocation or bypass a supported native form. Answers as soon as the runs are accepted, with a run id each - report those and stop; read ads_studio_get_run when the user asks, never in a loop. Generation takes a few minutes.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield_ads_studio_generate(args: {
  // Exact per-product counts from the Ads Studio app. Submit the whole allocation in one call, with brand_id, aspect_ratio and one stable idempotency_key. The first call quotes and requests approval without spending. Do not combine with product_ids, total, prompt, images, objective, include_brand or brand_kit. Chat-approved retries require expected_credits equal to the approved total cost.
  allocation?: Array<{
  count: number;
  // Display label only; authorization and allocation use product_id.
  name?: string;
  product_id: string;
}>;
  // The frame for the whole batch: 1:1 square feed, 9:16 stories and reels, 16:9 landscape, 3:4 portrait feed. 4:5 is not available - offer 3:4 as the nearest portrait frame.
  aspect_ratio?: "1:1" | "9:16" | "16:9" | "3:4";
  // The brand whose kit (logo, palette, tone) shapes the ads, from ads_studio_list_brands. Leave it out to make ads with no brand kit at all. The kit only reaches this brand's own products: a product of another brand, or of none, is advertised without it, so never promise the user this brand's look on someone else's product.
  brand_id?: string;
  // false to make the ads without the brand kit even though brand_id is set: a plain product or prompt ad. Default true when brand_id is set; always off without one.
  brand_kit?: boolean;
  // Exact credit cost explicitly approved by the user in chat. The server requotes before spending and refuses a changed price. For an app allocation on a host without native form support, preserve the exact allocation and key. Omit for native confirmation.
  expected_credits?: number;
  // A key you choose once for this generation and repeat unchanged if you have to retry. Never invent a new one for a retry: that buys the same batch a second time.
  idempotency_key: string;
  // Pictures the user supplied for this generation: inspiration or photos of their product.
  images?: Array<{
  // style (default): a look to follow. product: a photo of the thing being advertised.
  role?: "style" | "product";
  // A public https link to the picture.
  url: string;
}>;
  // Also generate a run about the brand itself, not a single product. Needs brand_id and the kit on.
  include_brand?: boolean;
  // What the ads are for. Set it only when the user made the goal clear (more sales -> sales; sign-ups, demos, quotes -> leads; visits, clicks -> traffic; a launch or being known -> awareness; comments, shares -> engagement). Left out, the product's own profile decides.
  objective?: "sales" | "leads" | "engagement" | "traffic" | "awareness";
  // Products to advertise, from ads_studio_list_products - of this brand, another brand or none; each gets its own run. Name at least one product, or set include_brand, or give a prompt - with none of them there is nothing to advertise.
  product_ids?: Array<string>;
  // What the user asked for in their own words: the angle, the offer, the audience. A prompt alone, with no product and no brand, is an ad about what it describes.
  prompt?: string;
  // How many concepts in total across all subjects: the number the user named, or 1 for a singular request. Ads Studio splits it between the subjects, so it must be at least one per subject.
  total?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Plans supported by Ads Studio.
  allowed_plans?: Array<string>;
  approval_required?: boolean;
  // The brand supplied for this generation, if any.
  brand_id?: string;
  // Total quoted credits for the exact allocation.
  credits?: number;
  // Credits available when the request was refused.
  credits_have?: number;
  // Credits required for the refused request.
  credits_needed?: number;
  // Credits missing for the refused request.
  credits_short?: number;
  error?: string;
  error_code?: string;
  // The concurrent-generation limit when the queue was full.
  limit?: number;
  next_step?: string;
  // On a partial start: the products whose runs did not start. Nothing was charged for them.
  not_started?: Array<{ name?: string; product_id?: string; }>;
  // On a partial start: why the rest did not start, when Ads Studio said.
  not_started_reason?: { code: string; message: string; [key: string]: unknown; };
  note?: string;
  // True when some runs started and others did not.
  partial?: boolean;
  // The account's current plan when access was refused.
  plan?: string;
  // The queued generation count when the queue was full.
  queued?: number;
  run_ids?: Array<string>;
  runs?: Array<{ concepts?: number; product_id?: string; run_id?: string; subject?: string; }>;
  // The products this batch advertises.
  selected_products?: Array<{ name?: string; product_id?: string; }>;
  started?: boolean;
}>>; };
```

