Read one Ads Studio generation run: its status and every concept in it, with the ad copy. Opens the generation card, which shows the pictures - there is no image link in the result and none to ask for. Call it when the user asks about a run - never on your own initiative and never in a loop. A run can read done while its pictures are still rendering, so check still_rendering before telling the user the ads are ready. A queued run carries its place in line; a canceled run stays canceled and is not a failure. Name a creative by its concept_id. These pictures are not ordinary generations: do not pass Ads Studio ids to show_generation_by_ids or jobs_wait.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield_ads_studio_get_run(args: {
  // Run id from ads_studio_generate or ads_studio_list_runs.
  run_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // Plans supported by Ads Studio.
  allowed_plans?: Array<string>;
  aspect_ratio?: string;
  brand_id?: string;
  concepts?: Array<{
  aspect_ratio?: string;
  // The id to name this creative by in Ads Studio.
  concept_id?: string;
  cta?: string;
  destination_url?: string;
  // The picture is ready and shows on the generation card.
  has_picture?: boolean;
  headline?: string;
  position?: number;
  primary_text?: string;
  render_error?: string;
  render_status?: string;
  status?: string;
}>;
  concepts_requested?: number;
  created_at?: string;
  credits?: { reserved?: number; settled?: number; };
  // Credits available when the request was refused.
  credits_have?: number;
  // Credits required for the refused request.
  credits_needed?: number;
  // Credits missing for the refused request.
  credits_short?: number;
  error?: string;
  error_code?: string;
  failed?: number;
  // The concurrent-generation limit when the queue was full.
  limit?: number;
  // The account's current plan when access was refused.
  plan?: string;
  product_id?: string;
  queue?: { plan_cap?: number; position?: number; };
  // The queued generation count when the queue was full.
  queued?: number;
  rendered?: number;
  rendering?: number;
  // Why the run failed, in ai-cmo's own words.
  run_error?: string;
  run_id?: string;
  stage?: string;
  status?: string;
  still_rendering?: boolean;
  subject?: string;
  waiting?: number;
}>>; };
```

