Execute a shell command in a remote Higgsfield cloud Linux sandbox — NOT your local machine or the client's own shell. Use it for Higgsfield media workflows and website_repo_access checkouts that require the hosted toolchain. Do not use it to inspect a local repository, install desktop software, or control applications on the user's computer. Preinstalled: ffmpeg/ffprobe, ImageMagick, sox, python3 with Pillow and faster-whisper, node/npm/npx, sharp-cli, Playwright with headless Chromium, caption fonts (Metropolis, Montserrat), zip/unzip, git, curl, jq. Use it for media processing (trim, convert, overlay, concat with ffmpeg), image manipulation, and packaging that dedicated Higgsfield tools do not cover. The sandbox is isolated per user. Existing sessions keep their assigned backend. E2B pauses with process memory; Modal preserves workspace files but not processes or RAM after replacement. Export important files within 24 hours of last use. A result with sandbox_created:true indicates a new sandbox, so files from earlier calls are not present; re-download missing inputs. It has internet access: bring files in with curl from media URLs (media_import_url or generation results). For an output created here, call media_upload BEFORE starting the producing command, then append `curl -f -X PUT --upload-file <file> '<upload_url>'` to that SAME command so the ephemeral file is uploaded before it exits; call media_confirm only after HTTP 200. Never pass a sandbox path to media_upload_and_confirm: that tool accepts only client attachments. Commands run in /home/user and time out after timeout_seconds (default 60, max 120); for longer work (large renders, installs) set background:true and poll the returned log/status files with later sandbox_exec calls. Background work is bounded to 15 minutes; follow the lifetime and polling guidance in the command result. Set restart:true to discard the sandbox and start clean. Set size:"xl" only for the heaviest CPU work, such as a final multi-job video render; omit it for downloads, probes, edits, polling and inspection. An XL request may move the workspace to a new larger sandbox (files kept, running processes not), and the XL sandbox shuts down about a minute after its work finishes. For actual visual inspection, pass image_paths (up to 4 PNG/JPEG paths, <=512 KiB total) with a foreground command: images are returned natively to the model, not as text or URLs. With background work, wait for completion then use a foreground poll with image_paths before its lease expires. No upload is needed for inspection. The command limit is 128000 characters including signed URLs; keep upload batches small and use installed scripts. Workflow bundle scripts are already installed in every sandbox under $HF_WORKFLOWS (/home/user/.higgsfield/workflows), laid out as $HF_WORKFLOWS/<workflow>/scripts/... — run them straight from there (they survive restart:true), and never paste script contents into the command.

