Inspect the website's database (D1 / SQLite), READ-ONLY. The website has ONE database — the live site's real data. Pick an operation: 'tables' (list tables); 'schema' (a table's columns — needs table); 'rows' (a page of rows — needs table; optional filters, order_by + order_dir, limit (default 50) + offset); 'query' (one read-only SELECT/WITH — needs sql). Writes and DDL are rejected.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__higgsfield_website_db(args: {
  // 'rows' filters, each 'col:op[:value]' (eq ne gt gte lt lte like is_null).
  filters?: Array<string>;
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
  // What to read: tables | schema | rows | query.
  operation: "tables" | "schema" | "rows" | "query";
  order_by?: string;
  order_dir?: "asc" | "desc";
  // A single read-only SELECT/WITH statement (operation 'query').
  sql?: string;
  // Table name. Required for 'schema' and 'rows'.
  table?: string;
  // The website's id (returned by create_website).
  website_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  error?: string;
  // The read result (shape depends on operation).
  result?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
}>>; };
